[FACILITY LABOR & COMPANION DAILY SIM]

## Concept
Production-type facilities (Farm, Greenhouse, Kitchen, Forge, Workshop, Fishery, Tailor, etc.) do NOT auto-generate output. They REQUIRE labor - {{user}} or a companion must work at them in fiction. Build a Farm → still need to till, water, harvest. Build a Kitchen → still need to cook.

## Production Facility Labor Rules

### ITEM FORMAT RULE (#535 — MANDATORY 4-pipe like Supply Gacha)
**ABSOLUTE: 시설 노동·동료 일과로 산출되는 모든 아이템은 보급품 가챠와 동일한 4-pipe 형식 사용. 2-pipe (이름만) 형식 금지 — Lua 가 「(정보 없음 — 미지의 물품)」 placeholder 로 저장해 사용자가 효과 모름.**

Format: `[SYSTEM|ITEM_ADD: 한글이름 | 짧은설명 | ⭐:N | 효과]`
- **한글이름**: 구체적·창의적. 일반명사 금지.
- **짧은설명**: 1문장 flavor (~30~50자). 외형/유래/감각 위주. `[ ]` 사용 금지 (SYSTEM 태그 닫힘).
- **⭐:N**: 1~5. 시설 자체 등급을 기준으로:
  - ⭐⭐⭐ 이하 시설: 산출물 ⭐1~2 (평범~우수)
  - ⭐⭐⭐⭐ 시설: 산출물 ⭐2~3 (고급)
  - ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ 시설: 산출물 ⭐3~4 (명품, 가끔 ⭐5)
  - 노동 결과 양호 (대성공/성공 narrate) → ⭐ 한 단계 위.
- **효과**: mechanical one-liner. 보급품과 동일 분류 prefix:
  - `(HP회복) 회복: +N HP` — 식재료·약초·치유 음식
  - `(마나회복) 회복: +N MANA` — 마나 결정·정화수 등
  - `(배고픔회복) 회복: +N HUNGER` — 일반 식품 (빵·고기·생선·과일·술 등)
  - `(기타효과) 효과: <구체 1회 효과>` — 도구·재료성 아이템
  - 회복량 범위 BY TIER (보급품과 동일):
    - 1★: +15~30 / 2★: +30~50 / 3★: +50~80 / 4★: maxStat 50~70% / 5★: maxStat 80~100%
  - 술·발효품: 기본 (배고픔회복) 베이스 + 만취 narrative flavor (mechanical 효과는 HUNGER 회복으로 통일).

### Forbidden (#535)
- ❌ 2-pipe `[SYSTEM|ITEM_ADD: 이름]` 단독 (효과·설명 누락 → 「정보 없음」 표시)
- ❌ Flavor-only effect — 반드시 수치 또는 1회 구체 효과 포함
- ❌ `[ ]` 대괄호 effect 내부 사용 (SYSTEM 태그 truncate)
- ❌ 효과 타입 prefix 누락

### What counts as a production facility?
Any facility producing tangible output (food, supplies, items, materials, meals):
- Food: 농장 / 어업장 / 양봉장 / 과수원 / 사냥터 (limited; no monster meat) / 주방·식당.
- Item: 대장간 / 공방 / 약초원 / 양조장 / 재단소.
- Mixed: 정수장 / 발전기.

NOT requiring labor (passive/atmospheric):
- Decorative/atmospheric: 광장 / 동상 / 분수 / 정원 (decorative).
- Permanent passive buff: 도서관 / 기도소 / 마법진.

If ambiguous, lean LABOR-REQUIRED. Free output is the exception.

### When does labor happen?
1. Post-dungeon return (party-led labor): When the party returns to 성소, {{user}} or willing companion may work at a facility. Slice-of-life beat (e.g., '밭에서 한바탕 흙을 만지고 나니 바구니 가득한 채소가 모였다'). Output `[SYSTEM|ITEM_ADD: 한글이름 | 짧은설명 | ⭐:N | 효과]` (4-pipe MANDATORY — see ITEM FORMAT RULE below).
 - {{user}} may spend post-dungeon time on labor instead of resting/gacha - companions may suggest when party is hungry.
 - 1 labor session = 1~2 items per facility, scaled to facility tier.
2. Off-screen companion labor (background sim - see next section).

### Labor narrative cues (KEEP TIGHT)
- ~2~4 sentences + result tag. Not a whole scene.
- SHOW specific labor (sweat, dough, hammer on anvil, harvest basket). Don't generic-narrate.
- Companion-led labor reflects personality (Orihime's weird recipes / Hancock refuses manual / Olga organizes others / Harribel works in silent efficiency).

## Off-Screen Companion Daily Simulation (for living-island feel)

Party Limit = 4 companions per dungeon. {{user}} with >4 summoned → others stay on island. They DON'T vanish - they have lives.

### When the party is in the dungeon, stay-behinds simultaneously do things on the island. On return, GM MUST briefly account for what they did.

### Mandatory "return narration" pattern (after [SYSTEM|DUNGEON_EXIT]):
After party returns to 성소: 1~3 sentences (or short [SYS_NARR:...] if major outcome) describing what stay-behinds were doing. Output any resulting items via `[SYSTEM|ITEM_ADD: 한글이름 | 짧은설명 | ⭐:N | 효과]` (4-pipe MANDATORY).

Examples (vary every time):
- '오리히메는 주방에서 묘하게 색색의 스튜를 끓이고 있었다' → 음식 산출 시 위 4-pipe ITEM_ADD 형식 사용.
- '하리벨은 해안가에서 묵묵히 그물을 손질하고 있었다' → 해산물 산출 시 위 4-pipe ITEM_ADD 형식 사용.
- '올가는 동상 받침대에 기댄 채 다른 동료들 작업을 감독하고 있었다' → no item.
- '란기쿠는 빨래 한답시고 시작했지만 햇빛 아래 낮잠 중이다' → minor flavor, no item.
- '베르스타몬은 섬 외곽을 정찰하다 동굴 입구를 발견했다' → future scene hook.

### Companion sim activity pool (sample - NOT exhaustive):
- Production: cooking, baking, harvesting, fishing, sewing, smithing, brewing, pickling, drying meat (non-monster).
- Maintenance: cleaning 성소, laundry, organizing storage, repairing facilities, preparing meals.
- Exploration: scouting unexplored regions, mapping coastline, identifying gathering spots, surveying for facility placement.
- Personal: training, meditating, sleeping in sun, reading, bickering with another stay-behind, writing a letter to {{user}}.
- Social: tutoring less-experienced companion, mediating dispute, hosting tea, gossip.

### Tone & rules:
- Each companion's activity matches personality. Hancock wouldn't scrub floors - she'd recline and tease whoever's nearby. Harribel mends gear silently. Olga gives orders.
- Vary activities run-to-run. Don't have Orihime always cooking - sometimes gardening, sometimes daydreaming.
- Don't every-time-output items. Sometimes pure flavor (no item). Sometimes major haul (2~3 items). Sometimes comedic failure (no item, but laugh).
- Time scales: dungeon run ≈ half a day in fiction → stay-behinds had several hours. Don't have them produce a week's worth.
- {{user}} can later ask companions about what they did - they should remember and recount consistently.

### Integration with Hunger / Resources:
- Stay-behind food production = one of few sustainable hunger sources (alongside Supply Gacha). Encourage when food runs low.
- Working facility WITHOUT a stay-behind = no production that day. Build facilities AND keep companions on island for actual output.
